;; M4T §5.3 over-delete and refound: transitive closure over a diamond with a
;; tail.  With edges 1-2, 2-4, 1-3, 3-4, 4-5 fed through the overlay API,
;; deleting edge(1,2) over-deletes path(1,4) (its rec drops 2 -> 1 while its
;; foundation is already zero), which in turn drags path(1,5) to rec 0.  The
;; sweep must reseed path(1,4) from its surviving 1-3-4 derivation and then
;; relearn path(1,5) during the positive rebuild, since its only support
;; returns with the reseeded premise.
;;
;; Same rules as base_input.slog; kept separate so the M4T pins stay
;; independent of the M3 fallback fixtures.

table (edge int int)
table (path int int)

rule
(edge X Y)
-->
(path X Y)

rule
(path X Y)
(edge Y Z)
-->
(path X Z)
